A||||11||Jay||The ultimate kit car!!!||||1||
Z||000000||Jay||05-15-2001||02:22 PM||||As mentioned in an earlier post, I jsut finished reading "Forza...the International magazine on Ferrari"  Wouldn't you know it?  There in the sacred pages of the worlds most renowned magazine on Ferrari is a kit car, well not in the typical sense.  A real Ferrari 308 was chopped and the space frame lengthened and reinforced to accept the longitudinaly mounted engine and transaxle.  The body was made to look like the 288 GTO.  But back to the engine.  It was not a Ferrari 2.8 liter like the 288 but rather a Chevy 511 cubic inch iron V8 with Dart alloy heads and twin Airesearch Super-60 diesel turbochargers, each the size of a space saver spare tire.  Total horsepower is 1600 at the wheels and 1829hp at the crank.  They've got the land speed record in their class at over 250mph and are aiming for the elusive 300mph next year.  Now that is a kit I wouldn't mind owning!!!!!!!Anyone got a conversion kit for sale?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Jay<BR>1986 northstar GT <A HREF="http://www.members.home.net/jaygrande" TARGET=_blank>www.members.home.net/jaygrande</A> ||||reg||1
